# Desktop shell, not a Hyprland rice

Do not pattern-match "Hyprland" to r/unixporn (keyboard-only, no dock, no icons, mod+key or nothing). That is the community default. Cicada is the opposite.

**Product:** GNOME/macOS-level *discoverability* (dock, desktop icons, click-to-Wi-Fi, notification center), with Hyprland **tiling as the default window layout**. Mouse launches and finds things. Keyboard tiling is there if you want it (go ham). Do not float every window. Do not make Super+key the only way to open an app.

Must exist and be clickable with a mouse, no hidden keybinds required:

- Wallpaper (hyprpaper and/or pcmanfm-qt desktop)
- Persistent left dock with pinned + running app icons (`nwg-dock-hyprland`)
- Desktop icons + drag-and-drop **and** file windows: `pcmanfm-qt` (one app, not a second file manager)
- Notification center (`swaync`), not toast-only
- One-click Wi-Fi, browser, files, settings
- Windows **tile** by default. Super+V floats one window. Launching is click, not a keybind exam.

Never ship a black canvas + terminals and call it a desktop. Never tell the user to "just use Super+Enter." Change skel/overlay and rebuild the ISO. Official repos only.
